eceived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rubueno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rubueno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rubueno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rubueno"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n * Bug Report\r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n~~~\r\nVR\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n~~~\r\nlatest\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n~~~\r\nN/A\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n~~~\r\nKVM\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n~~~\r\nWe have large customers with a lot of VR traffic traversing the VRs.  Logrotate cannot keep up and /var fills up to 100%, causing the VR to exhibit problems when attempting to start/restart instances in the VPC and/or traffic stops flowing.  Conntrackd is logging verbosely to daemon.log.\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n1. Construct a VPC with a redundant VR pair with a private gateway or tunnel\r\n2. Create a large amount of traffic to/from a VPC over gateway or tunnel\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n~~~\r\n/var should not fill up regardless of traffic load\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n~~~\r\n/var fills up\r\n~~~","comments":3,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6718/comments","created_at":"2022-09-08T22:58:16Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6718/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6718","id":1367074379,"labels":[{"color":"fc2929","default":false,"description":"","id":37843364,"name":"type:bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:bug"},{"color":"ffaaeb","default":false,"description":"","id":584073391,"name":"component:virtual-router","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzMzOTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:virtual-router"},{"color":