m/u/2486961?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DaanHoogland","id":2486961,"login":"DaanHoogland","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0ODY5NjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DaanHoogland"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"\u003c!--\r\nVerify first that your issue/request is not already reported on GitHub.\r\nAlso test if the latest release and main branch are affected too.\r\nAlways add information AFTER of these HTML comments, but no need to delete the comments.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\nSnapshot taking process should follow the following logic:\r\n\r\n1. If there are zero snapshots but there is a recurring schedule set, then it should still take the first snapshot for completion sake (regardless of whether Volume is detached or attached to a VM which is running or stopped).\r\n2. If there are existing snapshots, and the VM was up after the last snapshot, then take a snapshot (regardless of whether the VM is currently up or down or volume is detached since then)\r\n3. If there are existing snapshots, but the VM is currently down, AND the last snapshot was after the VM was shutdown, Skip the snapshot and then ADD EVENT - SKIPPING Snapshot for Volume ROOT-X/DATA-X indicating that it is skipped because VM is not running - this Event will help reduce future confusion when someone starts the server and thinks that bunch of days of snapshots are missing.\r\n\r\n\r\n##### ISSUE TYPE\r\n\u003c!-- Pick one below and delete the rest --\u003e\r\n  Bug Report \r\n\r\n##### COMPONENT NAME\r\n\u003c!--\r\nCategorize the issue, e.g. API, VR, VPN, UI, etc.\r\nUI, Snapshot\r\n--\u003e\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nNew line separated list of affected versions, commit ID for issues on main branch.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n4.17\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### CONFIGURATION\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the configuration if relevant, e.g. basic network, advanced networking, etc.  N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\r\n\u003c!--\r\nInformation about the environment if relevant, N/A otherwise\r\n--\u003e\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n##### SUMMARY\r\n\u003c!-- Explain the problem/feature briefly --\u003e\r\n\r\n\r\nUser has recurring snapshots on a Volume with KEEP 5 setting. \r\nThere are snapshots present already and 5 are seen in UI. \r\nUser shuts down the VM and leaves it off for several days. \r\nEach day, there is a ZERO size snapshot entry made, but in backend it points to the same last snapshot (checked via SQL).\r\nBut on Display there are tens of snapshots present and this counts against the MAX 100 snapshots per account (I know I can increase this to higher number). \r\nUsers are confused why so many snapshots. \r\n\r\nNOTE  - as a technical person, I understand why having the Zero size snapshot entry makes sense - essentially shows that the process ran as expected. However from user perspective, it is confusing especially when the server is down for weeks, and they come back to Max snapshots exceeded errors. \r\n\r\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\r\n\u003c!--\r\nFor bugs, show exactly how to reproduce the problem, using a minimal test-case. Use Screenshots if accurate.\r\n\r\nFor new features, show how the feature would be used.\r\n--\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste example playbooks or commands between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nUser has recurring snapshots on a Volume with KEEP 5 setting. \r\nThere are snapshots present already and 5 are seen in UI. \r\nUser shuts down the VM and leaves it off for several days. \r\nEach day, there is a ZERO size snapshot entry made, but in backend it points to the same last snapshot (checked via SQL).\r\nBut on Display there are tens of snapshots present and this counts against the MAX 100 snapshots per account (I know I can increase this to higher number). \r\nUsers are confused why so many snapshots. \r\n~~~\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- You can also paste gist.github.com links for larger files --\u003e\r\n\r\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What did you expect to happen when running the steps above? --\u003e\r\n\r\n~~~\r\n\r\n1. Zero size snapshots should not show up in the UI, and should not form a dependency in the cloud database's snapshot table. \r\nOR Perhaps indicate zero size snapshot in the UI so users know without contacting Admins.\r\n\r\n4. The zero size snapshots should not count against the Max 100 limit. \r\n~~~\r\n\r\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\r\n\u003c!-- What actually happened? --\u003e\r\n\r\n\u003c!-- Paste verbatim command output between quotes below --\u003e\r\n~~~\r\nzero size snapshots count against max snapshots.\r\nlarge number of snapshots in UI confuses the users\r\n~~~\r\n","comments":7,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6827/comments","created_at":"2022-10-14T03:23:24Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6827/events","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/6827","id":1408699817,"labels":[{"color":"84b6eb","default":false,"description":"","id":37843366,"name":"type:enhancement","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:enhancement"},{"color":"1D76DB","default":false,"description":"","id":4006883948,"name":"component:storage","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M7u1DJs","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:storage"},{"color":"E43179","default":false,"description":"","id":6890295339,"name":"status:stale","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABmrGQKw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/status:stale"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"id":9849008471,"name":"no-issue-activity","node_id":"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACSwvxVw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/no-issue-activity"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/6827/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":{"closed_issues":39,"created_at":"2026-05-08T06:15:20Z","creator":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57355700?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/weizhouapache","id":57355700,"login":"weizhouapache","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3MzU1NzAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/weizhouapache"},"description":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/milestone/47","id":15843055,"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47/labels","node_id":"MI_kwDOAJTq2M4A8b7v","number":47,"open_issues":274,"state":"open","title":"24.0","updated_at":"2026-10-02T08:13:00Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/milestones/47"},"node_i