[2026-10-02T13:36:57.474Z] [DEBUG] [rpc] github←resp 1770b {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"number\":2865,\"title\":\"DNS records for additional local IP addresses\",\"body\":\"##### ISSUE TYPE\\n * Feature Idea\\n\\n##### COMPONENT NAME\\n* DNS\\n\\n##### CLOUDSTACK VERSION\\n/\\n\\n##### CONFIGURATION\\n* for customer isolated network\\n\\n##### OS / ENVIRONMENT\\n/\\n\\n##### SUMMARY\\nFor adaptive computing it\\u0026#39;s important to get use of additional application local IP addresses which you can move between machines in case of a failure of one of the virtual machines or for upgrades.\\n\\nI can attach an additional IP to a VM using ACS. But I cannot give that a separate name which does not belong to the actual hostname of the VM.\\n\\n\\n##### STEPS TO REPRODUCE\\n\\n\\n##### EXPECTED RESULTS\\n* possibility to add a DNS name for the additional local IP address\\n* possibility to move an IP from one system to another (no delete and recreate - IP could be taken in the steps between)\\n\\n##### ACTUAL RESULTS\\n* currently the additional IP resolves into the same name as the original IP which is the hostname\",\"state\":\"open\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/2865\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"IngoJochim\",\"id\":38244286,\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/IngoJochim\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38244286?v=4\"},\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"labels\":[\"component:networking\",\"type:new-feature\",\"no-issue-activity\"],\"milestone\":\"unplanned\",\"comments\":5,\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"created_at\":\"2018-09-27T15:48:32Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-05-10T02:17:03Z\",\"issue_type\":\"Feature\"}"}]}}
